    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Pachycereus pringlei」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pachycereus_pringlei",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-12",
      "revision": 1370221601,
      "text": "Pachycereus pringlei is a species of large cactus native to northwestern Mexico, in the states of Baja California, Baja California Sur, and Sonora. It is commonly known as cardón, a name derived from the Spanish word cardo, meaning \"thistle\"; additionally, it is often referred to as sabueso, which is possibly an early Spanish colonialist interpretation of the Seri word for the plant, xaasj."
    }
